# oracle: kspace_style msm/dielectric with its default pressure/scalar yes (the scalar branch of lj/cut/coul/msm/dielectric: the tally carries the Coulomb part of the force, the LJ forces go to f at once and E_coul/3 joins the diagonal) and fix polarize/bem/icc every step, the two confined ions of examples/PACKAGES/dielectric moving (fix nve), boundary p p f, order 4, mesh 16 16 16, cutoff/adjust no, 4 steps.
# oracle-inputs: w71diel_confined.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 5.5e-14, atoms 1.0e-18.
units           lj
atom_style      dielectric
atom_modify     map array
dimension       3
boundary        p p f
read_data       w71diel_confined.data
group interface type 1
group ions type 2 3
group cations type 2
group anions type 3
set group cations epsilon 10
set group anions epsilon 10
pair_style      lj/cut/coul/msm/dielectric 1.122 10.0
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0
pair_coeff      1 1 0.0 1.0
kspace_style    msm/dielectric 0.0001
kspace_modify   order 4 mesh 16 16 16 cutoff/adjust no
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes one 5000
fix             1 ions nve
fix             3 interface polarize/bem/icc 1 1.0e-4
fix_modify      3 itr_max 50 dielectrics -10 15 1.0 0.866 NULL
thermo          2
thermo_style    custom step temp evdwl ecoul elong epair press
thermo_modify   flush yes format float %.15g
timestep        0.005
run             4
